    <profile name="Thunderhawk Cluster Bombs" id="6850-83e8-da91-9f31" hidden="false" typeId="a8b2-cae8-0cb2-0c83" typeName="Equipment">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">Each time the bearer ends a Normal move, you can select one enemy unit it moved over during that move and roll six D6: for each 3+, that unit suffers 1 mortal wound</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Aerial Assault" id="b866-3c97-5072-23ee" hidden="false" typeId="b139-9a8a-94a3-bdc7" typeName="Abilities">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="6468-b66d-4509-c7d6">Each time a unit with the Deep Strike ability disembarks from this model after it has made a Normal move, that unit is still eligible to declare a charge this turn.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Transport" id="b8a7-c187-b728-61af" hidden="false" typeId="9e43-915b-56bd-8ac5" typeName="Transport">
      <comment>Thunderhawk</comment>
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Capacity" typeId="b931-c943-fd09-3728">This model has a Transport capacity of 30. This model can embark up to two vehicle models. Vehicle models are treated as having Bulky (W)</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Damaged 13" id="b456-50e4-04dc-7edf" hidden="false" typeId="b139-9a8a-94a3-bdc7" typeName="Abilities">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="6468-b66d-4509-c7d6">While this model has 1-13 wounds remaining, each time this model makes an attack, subtract 1 from the Hit roll.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Deadly Demise D6+2" id="99dd-630b-fa7a-e64c" hidden="false" typeId="b139-9a8a-94a3-bdc7" typeName="Abilities">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="6468-b66d-4509-c7d6">Some models have &apos;Deadly Demise x&apos; listed in their abilities. When such a model is destroyed, roll one D6 before removing it from play (if such a model is a TRANSPORT, roll before any embarked models disembark). On a 6, each unit within 6&quot; of that model suffers a number of mortal wounds denoted by &apos;x&apos; (if this is a random number, roll separately for each unit within 6&quot;).</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
